# RTL (Right-to-Left) Support Rules

## Languages

- English: LTR (Left-to-Right)
- Hebrew: RTL (Right-to-Left)

## Implementation

Using React Native's `I18nManager`:

```typescript
import { I18nManager } from 'react-native';

const isRTL = language === 'he';
I18nManager.forceRTL(isRTL);
```

## Automatic Behavior

When Hebrew is selected:
- Text direction: RTL
- Layout direction: RTL
- Navigation: RTL
- Flexbox: RTL

## App Restart

RTL changes may require app restart to fully apply.

## Testing

Test both languages:
1. Switch to Hebrew in Profile screen
2. Verify text flows right-to-left
3. Verify navigation adapts
4. Verify layout mirrors correctly

## NativeWind & RTL

NativeWind automatically handles RTL:
- `ml-4` becomes `mr-4` in RTL
- `flex-row` reverses in RTL
- Text alignment adapts

## Best Practices

- Use logical properties (start/end) instead of left/right
- Test all screens in both languages
- Avoid hardcoded directional values
- Use flexbox for layouts (auto-adapts to RTL)
